id: pm-3mdmtd
title: "Accept only exact, time-bounded, owned advisory waivers in the dependency advisory gate, never for a package the published artifact installs"
description: "Interim mechanism for pm-03q389, decided by the owner on 2026-11-17: the dependency advisory gate (pm-eqxjzl) refused every branch and the daily release because GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf has no patched picomatch. config/dependency-advisory-waivers.json now declares waivers by GitHub advisory id, npm package and exact locked versions, with a pm owner, a reason and an RFC 3339 UTC expiry at most 30 days past the judging run. Receipt version 2 records validated registry advisory details; both feeds are covered only by exact live waivers; malformed, duplicate, expired, over-long and runtime-covering waivers refuse; the verdict discloses waived and unused waivers; the refusal now names the uncovered package@version advisory. The scheduled waiver-notice gate judges the same file, the notice window and that the owner is still open. A waiver never covers a package listed in runtime-dependencies.json, because consumers audit the published graph themselves (pm-gh1748 removed picomatch from that graph)."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: advisory-gate,dependency,release-blocker,security,waiver
